      "content": "7.1 Major Religious and Heritage Sites"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Pancharamas are five ancient holy shrines dedicated to Lord Shiva located across Andhra Pradesh.",
        "The five Pancharama sites are Amararama, Draksharama, Somarama, Ksheerarama, and Kumararama.",
        "UNESCO World Heritage Sites recognize monuments and natural sites of outstanding universal value.",
        "Temple architecture styles across heritage sites include Nagara, Dravida, and Vesara styles built under historic ruling dynasties."
